From: Karin-Laboratory <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: mediatek: propagate MT6990 SGMII PLL regmap failures

The MT6990 analog PHY's configure and power_on callbacks previously ignored
regmap_update_bits() failures, allowing a false successful configuration or
power-on when the shared PLL register was inaccessible. Check the first PLL
write before the cached configured fast path, remove the duplicate write,
and return the power_on error to the generic PHY caller.

Apply after 0002-air6-avoid-sgmii-top-cycle.patch to the exact pinned
GPL-2.0-only donor PHY source. Preserve the existing shared PLL/genpd
ownership and avoid a destructive SGMII TOP power cycle.

Build-only candidate. No hardware probe, injected MMIO fault, cold-boot,
redistribution approval or firmware signing is claimed.

--- a/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mt6990-sgmii.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mt6990-sgmii.c
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@
 static int mt6990_sgmii_phy_configure(struct phy *phy)
 {
 	struct mt6990_sgmii_phy *priv = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	int ret;
 
 	/* The SDK requires the shared PLL enable to remain asserted for the
 	 * complete SGMII active lifetime.  Reassert it even when the analog
@@ -66,8 +67,10 @@
 	 * table is already configured: another consumer of the shared AO
 	 * register bank must not leave a live port without its 3.125G clock.
 	 */
-	regmap_update_bits(priv->pll, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_CON0,
-			   MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN);
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(priv->pll, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_CON0,
+				 MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	if (priv->configured)
 		return 0;
@@ -74,10 +77,6 @@
 
 	dev_info(&phy->dev, "applying MT6990 SGMII Gen2 SerDes settings\n");
 
-	/* The analog XFI windows discard accesses until the shared PLL is on. */
-	regmap_update_bits(priv->pll, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_CON0,
-			   MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN);
-
 	/* Exact SDK mtk_sgmii_phy_gen2() sequence selected by the MT6990
 	 * CONFIG_MEDIATEK_NETSYS_V2=y kernel configuration.
 	 */
@@ -135,11 +134,9 @@
 	/* SDK mtk_sgmii_setup_mode_force() enables the shared PLL before any
 	 * per-port TOP/PCS operation and keeps it enabled while the link is up.
 	 */
-	regmap_update_bits(priv->pll, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_CON0,
-			   MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN);
-
 	/* The PCS releases SGMSYS_QPHY_PWR_STATE_CTRL later in .pcs_config(). */
-	return 0;
+	return regmap_update_bits(priv->pll, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_CON0,
+				  MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN, MT6990_SGMII_PLL_EN);
 }
 
 static int mt6990_sgmii_phy_set_mode(struct phy *phy, enum phy_mode mode,
